hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1148","Chapter on gifts of the polytheists, 1188 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl, from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of Tabuk until we reached Tabuk. Then the king of Aylah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and presented the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a white mule. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed him with a cloak and wrote for them concerning their sea."
"1149","1189 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Imran informed us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i, that he presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a she-camel - or he said: a gift - so he said to him: Have you accepted Islam? He said: No. He said: I have been forbidden the offerings of the polytheists. [Flag: parenthetical phrase about their gifts is an editorial insertion in one transmission.]"
